--- /dev/null
+++ b/CubeShim/docs/perf-trace.md
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# Host startup trace
+
+Set `CUBE_PERF_TRACE=1` in the process launching the shim. The shim's `start`
+process explicitly forwards this variable to its daemon. The flag is read once
+per process. Restart/recreate the process to change it; existing shims do not
+change their tracing mode. Any other value, including an unset variable, keeps
+the existing stat output schema and disables extra markers.
+
+With tracing enabled, `cube-shim-stat.log` records retain `CostTime` (integer
+milliseconds) and their existing attribution fields. They additionally contain:
+
+```json
+"PerfTrace": {
+  "SchemaVersion": 1,
+  "ClockId": "1234:1790000000000000000",
+  "OperationId": 7,
+  "Kind": "span",
+  "StartMonoNs": 100000,
+  "EndMonoNs": 100999,
+  "DurationNs": 999,
+  "DurationUs": 0,
+  "DroppedRecordsBefore": 0
+}
+```
+
+`DurationNs` and both monotonic endpoints derive from the same `Instant` and
+elapsed duration. `DurationUs` and legacy `CostTime` are truncated views, not
+separate measurements. The clock origin is first trace initialization within
+the process, not OS boot or wall time. Compare monotonic positions only within
+the same `ClockId`. The wall timestamp embedded in `ClockId` distinguishes
+process incarnations; it is not an accurate monotonic-to-wall-clock mapping.
+
+`OperationId` identifies an individual `StatDefer` scope within this clock.
+Existing `InstanceId`, `ContainerId`, `Action`, and `CalleeAction` provide
+attribution. No parent relationship is inferred or emitted.
+
+Task create emits additional `Kind: "cumulative"` records, using the task's
+same operation ID and start. Their `CalleeAction` values are:
+
+- `TaskCreate.LoadSpec`
+- `TaskCreate.AcquireSandboxLock`
+- `TaskCreate.CheckSandboxState`
+- `TaskCreate.InitSandbox` (only for a new sandbox)
+- `TaskCreate.StartSandbox`
+- `TaskCreate.CreateContainer`
+- `TaskCreate.PublishTaskEvent`
+
+These are checkpoints, not independent durations. Subtract adjacent checkpoints
+within the same clock and operation to obtain intervals; never add cumulative
+values. An interval includes any intervening log production, marker production,
+and other host work. For example, `AcquireSandboxLock - LoadSpec` includes the
+existing load-spec completion log before lock acquisition. It is not an isolated
+lock-wait measurement. Early failures may have only a prefix of checkpoints;
+the enclosing span retains its existing error status.
+
+`DroppedRecordsBefore` counts previously failed traced-stat serialization or
+nonblocking queue submissions in the process. It appears on subsequent records
+and cannot detect a lost final tail, file-write failure, or process crash.
+Validate sample coverage independently; zero is not proof of lossless logging.
+Tracing uses the existing asynchronous writer and may affect latency. Compare
+disabled and enabled runs before treating traced timings as the baseline.
+
+Run the logger and trace unit tests on Linux with the project builder:
+
+```sh
+cd CubeShim
+cargo test --locked -p containerd-shim-cube-rs log::
+cargo build --release --locked -p containerd-shim-cube-rs
+```
+
+This instruments host shim scopes already measured by `StatDefer`. It does not
+add timing inside guest restore or require a rebuilt template.
